Automatic Image Updates with OpenShift Image Change Triggers
Objective
Enable automatic updates of application pods by using image streams and image change triggers in OpenShift.
________________________________________
1. Image Stream Tags & Deployment Triggers
•	Image stream tags always point to an immutable SHA ID.
•	Updating a tag to a new image does not automatically update deployments.
•	To enable automatic rollout, configure the Deployment object with an image trigger.
•	Image triggers apply at the container level in a Deployment.
________________________________________
2. Configure Image Triggers for Deployment
Prerequisites
1.	Deployment uses image stream tags.
2.	Image stream in the same project.
3.	Local lookup enabled:
oc set image-lookup keycloak
4.	Deployment references image stream tag names (e.g., keycloak:20).
Steps
1.	Retrieve container names:
oc get deployment mykeycloak -o wide
2.	Add image trigger to container:
oc set triggers deployment/mykeycloak --from-image keycloak:20 --containers keycloak
3.	Verify trigger:
oc set triggers deployment/mykeycloak
•	AUTO=true indicates the trigger is active.
•	Stored in image.openshift.io/triggers annotation.
Manage Triggers
•	Disable:
oc set triggers deployment/mykeycloak --manual --from-image keycloak:20 --containers keycloak
•	Re-enable:
oc set triggers deployment/mykeycloak --auto --from-image keycloak:20 --containers keycloak
•	Remove all triggers:
oc set triggers deployment/mykeycloak --remove-all
________________________________________
3. Rolling Out Deployments
•	Deployment automatically updates when image stream tag changes.
•	Image stream tag can change:
o	Manually (oc tag or oc import-image).
o	Automatically with --scheduled refresh.
________________________________________
4. Managing Image Stream Tags
Create / Update Tags
1.	Initial creation:
oc create istag keycloak:20.0.2 --from-image quay.io/keycloak/keycloak:20.0.2
oc import-image keycloak:20.0.2 --from quay.io/keycloak/keycloak:20.0.2 --confirm
oc tag quay.io/keycloak/keycloak:20.0.2 keycloak:20.0.2
2.	Create alias tag:
oc tag --alias keycloak:20.0.2 keycloak:20
•	keycloak:20 is an alias → floating tag.
•	Deployment uses alias to track latest tested image.
Update to New Image
1.	Add new version:
oc create istag keycloak:20.0.3 --from-image quay.io/keycloak/keycloak:20.0.3
2.	Move alias to new version:
oc tag --alias keycloak:20.0.3 keycloak:20
•	Triggers automatic rollout for all Deployments using keycloak:20.
Rollback
oc tag --alias keycloak:20.0.2 keycloak:20
•	Resets Deployment to previous version.
________________________________________
5. Key Takeaways
1.	Image streams + triggers provide controlled, automatic application updates.
2.	SHA IDs ensure reproducibility.
3.	Aliases (floating tags) let you safely test and promote new versions.
4.	Rollback is simple by reassigning the alias to the previous image stream tag.
5.	Works for Deployments, Jobs, CronJobs, Pods.

